scope:
MEAS: independent review of the public score.json and four-page sheet pack (Alfred Cortot, acoustic transfer of a two-étude side: Op. 10 No. 5, then Op. 25 No. 9). Covers:
- the three token corrections (lines 91, 788, 1357), checked against first-edition page images;
- a converter re-run with --config, licence and attribution;
- bar order, gates and the sheet pack;
- the opening, the end and the display end;
- a register-aware per-bar lag scan, with pitch bands and onset lists over bars 59–72;
- reviewer overlays;
- reading the Concert Hall sheet-follow code for the part of the side after the score ends.
Not aural review; no browser run.

observations.finding:
This is non-blocking. The étude stays on black-key pentatonic material, so a chroma lag scan is near-flat: zero lag scores 0.613, and only 46 of 85 bars fit best within 0.3 s. The register-aware scan and pitch bands were used instead; it puts 65/85 bars within 0.1 s. Its 20 other bars:
- bars 12, 24, 28, 33, 34, 37, 38, 40, 48, 56, 58 and 80, with gains ≤1.15;
- bars 61 (+1.04 s, 1.30) and 82 (+1.04 s, 1.90): bars 61/62 and 81/82 have identical right hands, and the 85–96 s overlay shows bars 79–83 on the measured energy;
- bars 64 (−1.48 s, 1.17), 65 (−0.24 s, 1.41), 66 (+0.12 s, 1.70) and 70 (+0.08 s, 1.78): bars 64–65 land on the energy in the 63–72 s overlay;
- bars 67–69: see the defect.

report.finding:
The REPORT's figures match the config, receipt and public file:
- endpoint windows: first [3.6, 3.8] → 3.70 s; last [92.5, 92.8] → 92.666 s;
- endpoints.end 94.6 s, with its noise-gap basis;
- no constraints;
- the gates;
- score SHA-256 175bee75….
The candidate equals the public file; results equal checks; the config and audio hashes match. The REPORT's local-check claim for bars 63–68 is contradicted (see defect BARS_67_69_LIT_ABOUT_1S_EARLY).
